WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.160
How did Universal Studios know that this is what&nbsp;
the world looked like, especially from space?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.640
Okay, let's be clear; we had globes well before&nbsp;
we went to space. Like here's a globe from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:18.000
1400s. Not super accurate, but we had a globe. But&nbsp;
then look at this. These beauties are from 1862,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.320
well before we went to space. It's from a&nbsp;
French atlas that I like to just look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.180
because it's freaking gorgeous. But I mean, look&nbsp;
at the detail. This looks like the Earth. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:33.300
before we saw it from space. The fact is, we&nbsp;
knew what the Earth looked like because of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:39.960
lot of math and measurements. And we were&nbsp;
able to put that onto a sphere using this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.000
thing called projection. And it was all mathy and&nbsp;
cool. But yeah, we didn't need to go to space to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.860
do all this. We just had math and a bunch of smart&nbsp;
people working on this and that's how we did it.

